// REJECTS: Unsupported trigger type 'Weekly'
//
// `trigger:` is an ISLAND-typed field: `triggerSpecification: triggerType (triggerValue)?`
// where triggerType is just `identifier`. ANY identifier parses. The type name is then
// looked up among the registered trigger processors and `Manual` is the only one that
// resolves -- the switch in PersistenceParserExtension:66-80 names `Cron` too but returns
// null for it, so `trigger: Cron;` fails with this same message. IPersistenceParserExtension
// .process throws whenever the lookup produces nothing.
//
// So this is a WALKER rejection with no grammar involvement at all, and the failing token is
// a perfectly ordinary identifier. A parser derived from the .g4 has no way to refuse it --
// it has to carry the registry.
###Persistence
Persistence test::persistence::neg::InventedTrigger
{
  doc: 'a trigger type nobody registered';
  trigger: Weekly;
  service: test::persistence::Service;
  persister: Batch
  {
    sink: Relational
    {
      database: test::persistence::Database;
    }
    ingestMode: NontemporalSnapshot
    {
      auditing: None;
    }
    targetShape: Flat
    {
      modelClass: test::persistence::ModelClass;
      targetName: 'TestDataset1';
    }
  }
}
